  "text": "Their final Bridge presentation returned to the budget model Malik had repaired, expanded into a scenario for a first-year student managing books, meals, transportation, and emergencies. Malik explained the spreadsheet logic. Nia told the story of what happened when one assumption changed. They showed the original error, the revised categories, and a sensitivity table that made visible how quickly a small surprise could become a larger problem. A budget is not a promise that nothing will go wrong, Nia told the room. It is a way to notice change early enough to make choices. Malik advanced the slide. And a model should show what it assumes, so the person using it knows when the answer no longer applies. Dr. Brooks smiled from the back row.",
